 "Antidepressants that boost serotonin and noradrenaline. Effective for depression and anxiety, but stopping suddenly causes notorious withdrawal symptoms.",
 "Venlafaxine and desvenlafaxine treat depression and anxiety disorders and can reduce menopausal hot flushes. They take 2 to 6 weeks to work. Missing doses or stopping quickly often causes dizziness, ‘brain zaps’ and irritability, so doses are reduced slowly.",
 [("For", "Depression, generalised anxiety, social anxiety, panic disorder; hot flushes (off-label)"),
  ("Works", "Similar to other antidepressants"),
  COST,
  ("Kicks in", "2 to 6 weeks"),
  ("Dose", "Venlafaxine 75 to 225 mg daily; desvenlafaxine 50 to 100 mg daily"),
  ("Watch for", "Nausea, sweating, sleep changes, higher blood pressure; withdrawal if doses are missed")],
 "Effective, with a sting in the tail if you stop fast.",
 ["Venlafaxine: Efexor-XR, Enlafax XR, Elaxine SR. Desvenlafaxine: Pristiq, Desfax, Desven"],
 "SNRIs block reuptake of serotonin and noradrenaline, increasing their signalling between nerve cells.",
 ["Major depression", "Generalised anxiety, social anxiety and panic disorder", "Hot flushes when hormone therapy isn’t suitable (off-label)", "Some nerve pain (duloxetine is the SNRI more often used)"],
 "Many early side effects settle in 1 to 2 weeks.",
 [g(V, ["Nausea", "Sweating"]), g(C, ["Insomnia or drowsiness", "Dry mouth, constipation", "Headache, dizziness", "Sexual side effects", "<b>Raised blood pressure</b> (higher doses)"]), g(U, ["Low sodium in older people"]), g(R, ["<b>Serotonin syndrome</b> with other serotonergic drugs", "<b>Suicidal thoughts in under-25s when starting</b>"])],
 ["Thoughts of suicide or self-harm: call Lifeline 13 11 14 or 000", "Agitation, fever, shaking and muscle jerks (serotonin syndrome)", "Severe headache with very high blood pressure"],
 ["Take at the same time daily, with food.", "Don’t stop suddenly: taper with your doctor, sometimes over weeks to months.", "Check blood pressure.", "Avoid St John’s wort, tramadol and other serotonergic medicines unless checked."],
 [("What is venlafaxine withdrawal like?", "Dizziness, ‘brain zaps’, nausea, irritability and vivid dreams, sometimes within a day of a missed dose. Slow tapering reduces this."),
  ("Is desvenlafaxine the same as venlafaxine?", "Desvenlafaxine is the active substance venlafaxine turns into. They work similarly."),
  ("Does venlafaxine help hot flushes?", "Yes, it reduces flushes, though less than hormone therapy.")],
 [BB, ("PBS: Venlafaxine", PBS + "venlafaxine")],
