 ["Low mood, anxiety or thoughts of self-harm: stop and get help", "Severe headache with vision changes", "Pregnancy, or a missed period"],
 ["Use effective contraception for 1 month before, during and 1 month after treatment, with pregnancy tests.", "Don’t combine with doxycycline or other tetracyclines.", "Use lip balm and moisturiser constantly; avoid waxing and laser.", "Don’t donate blood during treatment."],
 [("Does Roaccutane cause depression?", "Mood changes have been reported, though large studies give mixed results. Any mood change should be reported, and treatment stopped if needed."),
  ("How long is a Roaccutane course?", "Usually 4 to 8 months, depending on dose and response."),
  ("Can a GP prescribe isotretinoin?", "In Australia it’s usually started by a dermatologist. Rules differ between states.")],
