 "It blocks alpha-1A receptors in the prostate and bladder neck muscle.",
 ["Enlarged prostate (benign prostatic hyperplasia)", "Helping ureteric stones up to about 10 mm pass (off-label)", "Combined with dutasteride or finasteride for larger prostates"],
 "Usually mild.",
 [g(C, ["Dizziness, especially standing up", "<b>Reduced or no ejaculate</b>", "Stuffy nose"]), g(U, ["Fainting", "Palpitations"]), g(R, ["<b>Floppy iris syndrome</b> during cataract surgery", "Prolonged painful erection"])],
 ["Unable to pass urine: emergency", "Fainting", "Erection lasting over 4 hours"],
 ["Stand up slowly, especially with the first doses.", "Tell your eye surgeon before cataract surgery.", "Swallow capsules whole.", "See your doctor yearly to review symptoms and need."],
 [("How long does tamsulosin take to work?", "Many men notice better flow within a few days, with the full effect in 2 to 4 weeks."),
  ("Does tamsulosin affect ejaculation?", "Commonly, it reduces or stops ejaculate fluid. It’s harmless and reverses on stopping."),
  ("Does tamsulosin help kidney stones?", "It can help larger stones (about 5 to 10 mm) in the lower ureter pass.")],
 [("Healthy Male", "https://www.healthymale.org.au/"), ("PBS: Tamsulosin", PBS + "tamsulosin")],
